# Agibot A3 deploy example (vendor package). We DO track the source/configs/docs
# here -- including our a3_pingpong sim-to-real port. Only the multi-GB build
# outputs, bundled third-party libs, model/mesh assets, and logs are ignored.
# Stray binaries (*.onnx/*.so/*.pt/...) are already covered by the global rules below.
agi/a3_deploy_example/build/
agi/a3_deploy_example/dist/
# thirdparty: ignore the big vendor bundles (onnxruntime 118M, unitree_sdk2 81M,
# rknn runtime, .deb) BUT track joint_msgs -- 40 KB of .msg/CMake sources that the
# deploy package build AND the hope_ws ROS chain (agibot_hardware_bridge, wbc_runner
# hardware mode) depend on. A blanket thirdparty/ ignore made fresh clones unbuildable.
agi/a3_deploy_example/thirdparty/*
!agi/a3_deploy_example/thirdparty/joint_msgs/
# assets: ignore models/motions (binary, 175M+) but keep the README that documents them.
agi/a3_deploy_example/assets/*
!agi/a3_deploy_example/assets/a3_runtime/
agi/a3_deploy_example/assets/a3_runtime/*
!agi/a3_deploy_example/assets/a3_runtime/README.md
agi/a3_deploy_example/mujoco_sim_standalone/
agi/a3_deploy_example/logs/
agi/a3_deploy_example/.github/

# Large vendor/runtime artifacts kept outside normal git history.
*.onnx
*.rknn
*.engine
*.trt
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.tar.gz
*.deb
*.so
*.a
